> 1 > set the resumeMAC-I to the 16 least significant bits of the MAC-I calculated:  
> 2 > over the ASN.1 encoded as per clause 8 (i.e., a multiple of 8 bits) VarResumeMAC-Input;  
> 2 > with the K key in the UE Inactive AS Context and the previously configured integrity protection RRCint algorithm;  
> and 2 > with all input bits for COUNT, BEARER and DIRECTION set to binary ones;

From this, the value provided by RRC to lower layers for the 5-bit BEARER parameter is **binary ones** (i.e., all bits set to 1). This is explicitly stated in the clause.

